  "system": {
    "description": "<p>A calling for one who would harness wild and ancient might.</p><p></p><p> Magic is often pursued through ravenous study, but not every magician learns the art hunched over a dusty tome. Before the first feather had been made a quill, some learned magic by studying the creaking of pines, the howling of wind, the crackling of flame. These secrets remain for those with the cunning to hear them.</p><p></p><p>Let the earth be your teacher, and its harsh lectures shall impart on you its power. In time, the wrath of the natural world will be yours to command, its wisdom is yours to learn, and its domain yours to protect or to exploit. To whatever end you direct its might, take caution: invoking the elements is a wilder practice than the precise methods of scholarly magic. Such primal forces demand a soul as hale and unflagging as the land itself.</p>",
